          {
            "id": 2807437,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "New members often say to me that they've been put off running either because they lack confidence or they don't have time or they think they dislike running. Kerry, for example, joined the club two years ago at the age of 40. She'd always enjoyed running at school, but wasn't sure if she'd be able to do it. She was worried about being left behind and being the slowest runner. But she says she was made to feel so welcome, she soon forgot all about that.",
